  "articleBody": "When you're tackling door frame modifications, there are a few common pitfalls that can turn a simple fix into a headache. One of the biggest mistakes is ignoring misalignment. If the frame isn't perfectly square, plumb, and level, your door will never operate correctly, leading to binding or gaps. Another common error? Failing to double-check the opening dimensions and hardware spacing. You might end up with a door that's too big or too small, or hardware that just doesn't line up. People also often leave rough edges that can interfere with the latch operation, making the door hard to close. And, unfortunately, it’s easy to underestimate damage that extends beyond the frame into the surrounding wall framing. If you're dealing with rot, structural issues, or anything complex, it's really smart to get a professional's input. We can help ensure those tricky parts are handled correctly, preventing bigger, more expensive problems later on.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}